{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"0b26f544d9e6d2317ef88a430b981cccf67d75a6cdc0620552879df567a16552","packTokens":4047,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":3986,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall implement every HTTP operation in contracts/openapi.yaml with its declared method, path, parameters, request and response schemas, security requirements, success and error statuses, and behavior, without deviation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid request for any method and path declared in contracts/openapi.yaml, with the declared authentication and permission requirements satisfied, or the declared unauthenticated sign-in operation used as specified. when A client sends the request to the API. then The response status and JSON fields match the operation's declared success response schema and behavior.\",\n    \"Given A request to a declared operation has missing or invalid credentials, insufficient permission, or input rejected by a declared validation or conflict rule. when A client sends the request to the API. then The response status and error fields match the corresponding statuses and schemas declared for that operation.\",\n    \"Given Valid inputs, existing resources where required, and an authorized principal for each listed operation: POST /api/auth/sign-in (200, SignInResponse); GET /api/session (200, SessionResponse); GET /api/dashboard (200, DashboardResponse); GET /api/imports/source-records (200, ImportPreviewResponse); POST /api/imports (200, ImportResult); GET and PUT /api/allocations (200, AllocationsResponse); GET /api/lots (200, LotsResponse); GET /api/lots/{lotId}/forecast (200, ForecastResponse); PATCH /api/forecast-settings and PATCH /api/lots/{lotId}/forecast-settings (200, ForecastSettingsResponse); GET /api/lots/{lotId}/metrics (200, LotMetricsResponse); GET /api/lots/{lotId}/insights (200, InsightsResponse); POST /api/lots/{lotId}/insights/actions (200, InsightActionResponse); GET /api/lots/{lotId}/weights (200, WeightHistoryResponse); POST /api/lots/{lotId}/weights (201, WeightMeasurementResponse); GET /api/inventory (200, InventoryResponse); POST /api/inventory/items (201, InventoryItemResponse); PATCH /api/inventory/items/{itemId} (200, InventoryItemResponse); POST /api/inventory/movements (201, MovementResponse); GET /api/inventory/projections (200, ProjectionsResponse); GET /api/inventory/export (200, ExportResponse with text/csv artifact); GET /api/rations (200, RationsResponse); POST /api/rations (201, RationResponse); PATCH /api/rations/{rationId} (200, RationResponse); POST /api/rations/optimization (200, OptimizationResponse); POST /api/rations/{rationId}/approval (200, ApprovalResponse); GET /api/feed-plans (200, FeedPlansResponse); POST /api/feed-plans (201, FeedPlanResponse); POST /api/feed-plans/{planId}/review and PATCH /api/feed-plans/{planId}/status (200, FeedPlanResponse); GET /api/feeding-events (200, FeedingEventsResponse); POST /api/feeding-events (201, FeedingEventResponse); PATCH /api/feeding-events/{eventId} and POST /api/feeding-events/{eventId}/void (200, FeedingEventResponse); GET /api/reports/operational (200, OperationalReportResponse); GET /api/reports/operational/export (200, ExportResponse with text/csv artifact); GET /api/reports/feed-to-gain (200, FeedToGainResponse); GET /api/reports/feed-to-gain/export (200, ExportResponse with requested csv or pdf artifact); GET /api/reports/profitability (200, ProfitabilityResponse); GET /api/reports/profitability/export (200, ExportResponse with text/csv artifact); GET /api/sample-data (200, SampleDataResponse); POST /api/sample-data/load, /api/sample-data/reset, and /api/sample-data/replace (200, SampleOperationResponse). when A client sends valid requests to each listed method and path, using the specified input, filters, and permissions. then Each response status and response body conform to the listed status and response schema, and each export response contains the declared file artifact.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall persist all application values its operations read or change, including derived or cached values used by later requests, in PostgreSQL through the existing App connection string, make committed values available to later requests and after restart, and initialize required application structures without deleting or changing compatible pre-existing data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A PostgreSQL database configured through the App connection string contains a compatible pre-existing row and the application starts. when The application initializes its database structures and a contract operation reads or changes application data. then The pre-existing row remains in the database, and the response reflects persisted data after the request.\",\n    \"Given A contract operation creates or changes application data, including a value differing from the existing value. when The API completes the operation successfully. then The corresponding database row contains the submitted values and derived or cached values returned in the response.\",\n    \"Given A successful API mutation has been committed to the configured PostgreSQL database. when The API process restarts and a contract read operation retrieves that data. then The response fields contain the committed values from the database row.\",\n    \"Given A clean PostgreSQL database is configured through ConnectionStrings:App and an authorized principal can create or change an application record. when The client uses the contract operation and then reads the record through the corresponding API list or detail operation. then The response contains the saved value and a PostgreSQL row contains the same value.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true at application startup on an initially clean database, the Feedlot Operations API shall run App.Api/SeedData.cs to populate each application table with demo rows based on believable examples from contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A clean database is configured and Seed:Demo is true. when The application starts and a client requests each contract list operation. then Each response list count is at least one and the returned sample values include data drawn from contract examples.\",\n    \"Given The App database is empty and Seed:Demo is true. when The application starts and database-backed list operations are requested. then Each application-data table contains 1–3 rows derived from contract examples, and the response lists show those sample values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true on a clean database, the Feedlot Operations API shall populate each application table with two or three believable sample rows based on examples in contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A clean PostgreSQL database and application configuration Seed:Demo=true. when The application starts and a test queries the application tables and calls their corresponding list API operations. then Each application table has two or three sample rows and each list response contains at least one corresponding row.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, the Feedlot Operations API shall not run SeedData.Run or insert demo rows during application startup, and shall serve contract operations without requiring demo seed rows to exist.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Seed:Demo is false and the database has no operational rows. when A client calls contract operations valid for an empty data state. then The response status and fields conform to the contract without requiring a seeded record.\",\n    \"Given The App database is empty and Seed:Demo is false. when The application starts and its database-backed list operations are requested. then Every application-data table has a demo row count of zero, and the response lists contain no demo-seeded records.\",\n    \"Given A clean PostgreSQL database and application configuration Seed:Demo=false. when The application starts and a test queries the application tables and calls list API operations. then The demo-data row count is zero and the list responses contain no demo rows.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall remain a backend API and documentation surface and shall not add product-facing web application screens or frontend implementation in this repository.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The repository implementation is complete. when A person reviews its exposed web surfaces and frontend files. then The review finds API and API documentation surfaces but no product-facing screens or frontend implementation.\",\n    \"Given The API application built from this repository. when A person inspects its browser-accessible surfaces. then The screen shows API health or API documentation and does not show feedlot product screens.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a ration defines ingredient proportions, the Feedlot Operations API shall calculate ingredient consumption and ration cost from as-fed ingredient weights and use dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A ration contains ingredients with stated proportions, different dry-matter percentages, and known unit costs. when A client records a feeding event and reads the ration and event results. then The response ingredient movement quantities and cost fields reflect the as-fed proportions and costs, while nutritional values reflect dry-matter values.\",\n    \"Given A ration has two ingredients with known as-fed unit costs and dry-matter percentages, with proportions of 70% and 30%, and a feeding request delivers 100 lb. when The feeding event is recorded successfully. then The response movement fields report 70 lb and 30 lb consumed, its cost fields equal the as-fed weighted cost, and its nutritional fields reflect the ingredients' dry-matter conversion.\",\n    \"Given A test-created ration whose ingredient proportions are percentages of as-fed weight, with different dry-matter percentages and known unit costs, and sufficient inventory. when The client records a feeding event through POST /api/feeding-events. then The response event shows each ingredient's consumed as-fed quantity and a cost equal to the sum of as-fed ingredient quantities multiplied by their unit costs, while nutrition values reflect dry-matter data.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a feeding event requires more of any ration ingredient than is available in inventory, the Feedlot Operations API shall reject the entire event without changing inventory or feed rollups.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An ingredient has less available inventory than a proposed feeding event requires and inventory and lot rollup values have been recorded. when The client posts the feeding event. then The response status is 409 and the inventory row, feeding-event row count, and lot feed totals remain unchanged.\",\n    \"Given Inventory contains less than the required quantity of at least one ingredient for a feeding event. when A client submits the event to the createFeedingEvent operation. then The response status is 409, no feeding-event row or inventory-movement row is added, and inventory quantities and lot feed and cost rollup values remain unchanged.\",\n    \"Given A test-created ration and inventory where one ingredient has less stock than the event requires, with recorded pre-request inventory and lot totals. when The client submits POST /api/feeding-events for that event. then The response status is 409, no event row exists for the rejected request, the inventory row values are unchanged, and the lot feed-total response values are unchanged.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Days on Feed is zero, the Feedlot Operations API shall return ADG as null; when a weight-gain denominator is nonpositive it shall return feedConversionRatio and costOfGain as null; and when ADG is nonpositive or no positive gain remains toward the target it shall return projectedShipDate as null. Affected feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship dates shall be unavailable whenever their required denominator or positive gain is absent.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A lot has zero Days on Feed, or has zero or negative total weight gain or ADG. when The client requests that lot's metrics. then The response fields for affected metrics and projectedShipDate contain null rather than a numeric value or date.\",\n    \"Given A lot has zero Days on Feed. when A client reads its lot metrics and lot list values. then The response adg and projectedShipDate fields are JSON null.\",\n    \"Given A lot has positive Days on Feed and zero or negative total weight gain. when A client reads its lot metrics, lot list, dashboard, and feed-to-gain report values. then The response adg, feedConversionRatio or fcr, costOfGain or costPerGain, and projectedShipDate fields are JSON null wherever those fields are exposed.\",\n    \"Given A lot has positive Days on Feed and positive total weight gain below its target weight. when A client reads its lot metrics after the latest weight measurement is recorded. then The response contains numeric values for applicable feed-to-gain metric fields and a projectedShipDate field calculated from the positive gain rate.\",\n    \"Given A test-created lot whose receiving date makes Days on Feed zero. when The client sends GET /api/lots/{lotId}/metrics. then The response field daysOnFeed is 0 and the response fields adg and projectedShipDate are null.\",\n    \"Given A test-created lot with positive Days on Feed and zero or negative total weight gain. when The client sends GET /api/lots/{lotId}/metrics. then The response fields feedConversionRatio and costOfGain are null, and projectedShipDate is null when ADG is zero or negative.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Every HTTP method and path declared in the locked OpenAPI contract conforms to its declared request, response, status, and security definitions.\",\n  \"Committed application state is durable, compatible pre-existing database rows are preserved during startup schema initialization, and compatible pre-existing application data is not removed.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}